        "<h4>Monte Carlo Integration Method to Estimate Pi</h4>\n",
        "Code originally created by Balthazar Courvoisier and posted on Quants Quest website\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "(https://quants.quest/PiEstimation/)\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "Specific question: How does the error of the Monte Carlo integration method change based on the number of samples taken when estimating pi?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "id": "4ee61666-1378-4ca1-bb88-ee039cf33772",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4ee61666-1378-4ca1-bb88-ee039cf33772"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def est_pi(iter):\n",
        "\n",
        "    n = int(iter)  # number of simulations\n",
        "    x1 = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, n)\n",
        "    x2 = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, n)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Check which points fall inside the unit circle\n",
        "    inside_circle = x1**2 + x2**2 <= 1\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Estimate of pi\n",
        "    pi_estimate = 4 * inside_circle.mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "    return pi_estimate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "id": "bbec5f19-7591-4957-963e-73e8cfa592f9",
      "metadata": {
