        "How do Monte Carlo, trapezoid, and Simpson compare for the same function?\n",
        "### Function:  𝑓(𝑥)=𝑒^𝑥\n",
        "### Interval:  [0,1]\n",
        "### Exact answer:  𝑒−1\n",
        "### Same number of function evaluations per run: 101\n",
        "### Tolerance: 0.00005\n",
        "### Monte Carlo: repeat 100 times and compare its mean absolute error\n",
        "Code originally created by\n",
        "\n",
        "（https://github.com/Inf1n1ty-8/Applied-Math-Python-Portfolio/blob/main/02_numerical_integration.ipynb）\n",
        "(https://people.duke.edu/~ccc14/sta-663/MonteCarlo.html)  \n",
        "\n",
        "(HW 3 and HW 6)\n",
        "\n",
        "Specific question: How does the error change based on the method of integration for a given function?"
